-- **Strengths:** Differentiable, real-time rendering, handles complex scenes with millions of Gaussians.
-- **Limitations:** Sorting is required for correct alpha compositing, which can be expensive. Degenerate Gaussians (zero scale) can cause numerical instability.
-- **When to use:** Real-time rendering, differentiable rendering for optimization.
-- **When not to use:** Scenes with extreme self-occlusion where order-independent transparency is critical (though Hybrid Transparency addresses this).
