 ## Background
-3D Gaussian Splatting Rasterization is the core rendering engine for 3D Gaussian Splatting, a method introduced by Kerbl et al. in 2023 [S2, unofficial]. It represents a scene as a collection of 3D Gaussians and rasterizes them to 2D images by projecting 3D covariances to 2D screen covariances, sorting by depth, and compositing colors based on alpha and transmittance [S2, unofficial]. The method has been ported to various platforms, including MLX (Apple Silicon) [S1, unofficial] and PyTorch/CUDA [S2, unofficial].
